You are fixing a bug in a Go repository (github.com/labstack/echo/v4) checked out at /echo. Work ONLY on /echo/context.go. Do not modify any other file, do not add test files to the repo permanently, and do not modify existing tests.

BUG: `func (c *context) Scheme() string` in /echo/context.go (around line 252) currently returns the raw value of the forwarded scheme headers without validating it:

```go
func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}
```

EXPECTED BEHAVIOUR (this is what the hidden tests check): invalid values in these forwarded headers must be IGNORED, i.e. the code must continue to the next header, and if none of the headers carries a valid scheme the function must fall back to "http". Concretely, the hidden test has subtests named "ignores invalid X-Forwarded-Proto and uses X-Forwarded-Protocol" (X-Forwarded-Proto set to an invalid value, X-Forwarded-Protocol set to a valid one -> returns the X-Forwarded-Protocol value) and "ignores invalid forwarded headers and falls back to http" (all four headers set to invalid values -> returns "http").

REQUIRED FIX: treat a forwarded scheme header value as valid only if it is `"http"` or `"https"` (exact, case-sensitive comparison, consistent with the neighbouring `ssl == "on"` check). Rewrite Scheme() as:

```go
func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme == "http" || scheme == "https" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}
```

Do not change anything else in context.go.

VERIFICATION (all of it):
1. `cd /echo && gofmt -l context.go` (must print nothing), `cd /echo && go build ./... && go vet ./...`.
2. Create a TEMPORARY test file /echo/context_zz_tmp_test.go (package echo) with test `TestTmpSchemeValidation` that asserts, using github.com/stretchr/testify/assert and net/http/httptest:
   - req with Header "X-Forwarded-Proto" = "invalid" and "X-Forwarded-Protocol" = "https" -> c.Scheme() == "https"
   - req with "X-Forwarded-Proto"="invalid", "X-Forwarded-Protocol"="invalid", "X-Forwarded-Ssl"="invalid", "X-Url-Scheme"="invalid" -> "http"
   - req with "X-Forwarded-Proto"="https" -> "https"; "X-Forwarded-Protocol"="http" -> "http"; "X-Forwarded-Ssl"="on" -> "https"; "X-Url-Scheme"="https" -> "https"; no headers -> "http"
   - req with TLS set (httptest.NewRequest("GET", "https://example.com/", nil)) -> "https"
   Use `e := echo.New(); c := e.NewContext(req, httptest.NewRecorder())`.
   Run `cd /echo && go test . -run TestTmpSchemeValidation -v -count=1` and report the output.
3. Run the pre-existing tests that matter: `cd /echo && go test . -run 'TestContext' -v -count=1 2>&1 | tail -40` and the FULL suite `cd /echo && go test ./... -count=1 2>&1 | tail -20`. Report exact failures (there must be none).
