Go repo github.com/labstack/echo/v4 at /echo. Fix a bug in /echo/bind.go ONLY (do not touch other files, do not modify existing tests).

BUG: `func (b *DefaultBinder) bindData` has a map branch:
```go
	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		for k, v := range data {
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
		}
		return nil
	}
```
This panics when the destination map's value type is a slice (e.g. `map[string][]string`), because a `string` is not assignable to `[]string`.

HIDDEN TEST: `TestDefaultBinder_bindDataToMap` with subtest `ok, bind to map[string][]string` must pass. Expected behaviour: binding data (e.g. query params `?foo=bar&foo=baz`) into a `map[string][]string` destination (either directly via `BindQueryParams(c, &m)` or into a struct field with a tag) must succeed and store the FULL value slice for each key, e.g. `map[string][]string{"foo": {"bar","baz"}}`. Binding into `map[string]string` must keep working (first value).

FIX: in the map branch, if the map's element type is a slice, set the whole `v`; otherwise set `v[0]`:
```go
	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		for k, v := range data {
			if typ.Elem().Kind() == reflect.Slice {
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v))
			} else {
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
			}
		}
		return nil
	}
```

VERIFY: `cd /echo && gofmt -l bind.go` (empty), `go build ./... && go vet ./...`. Write a TEMPORARY test /echo/zz_tmp_bindmap_test.go (package echo) named `TestTmpBindDataToMap` covering: (1) `m := map[string][]string{}` + `BindQueryParams` on request `/?foo=bar&foo=baz` -> `{"foo":{"bar","baz"}}`; (2) `m := map[string]string{}` + `/?foo=bar&foo=baz` -> `{"foo":"bar"}`; (3) a struct with `Foo map[string][]string \`query:"foo"\`` field bound via BindQueryParams. Run `go test . -run TestTmpBindDataToMap -v -count=1` and report. Then run the full suite `go test ./... -count=1 2>&1 | tail -20` (must be all ok). Then DELETE the temp file, re-run the full suite, and run `git status --porcelain` (must show only modified files: bind.go, context.go, middleware/proxy.go; no untracked files).

REPORT: final `git diff bind.go`, test outputs, failing test names if any, git status.

Go repo github.com/labstack/echo/v4 at /echo. Find and fix ONE injected bug in /echo/middleware/compress.go. Do not modify other files; do not modify existing tests.

CLUE: a hidden test named `TestGzipEmpty` (package middleware) must pass after the fix. It tests the Gzip middleware with an EMPTY response body: when the handler writes no body (e.g. `return c.NoContent(http.StatusOK)` or a 204/304 response), the response must stay pristine — the gzip header must NOT be written, `Content-Encoding` must not be set, and the body must remain empty. The known upstream implementation guards this in the deferred cleanup:
```go
				defer func() {
					if res.Size == 0 {
						// We have to reset response to it's pristine state when
						// nothing is written to body or error is returned.
						// See issue #424, #407.
						res.Writer = rw
						w.Reset(ioutil.Discard)
					}
					w.Close()
					pool.Put(w)
				}()
```
Read /echo/middleware/compress.go fully and compare with that; the injected bug is likely a subtle deviation there (wrong condition, missing reset, wrong order of Close/Reset, wrong writer restored, gzip header written eagerly, etc.).

METHOD:
